[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

A temperature overhaul for [b]Build 42[/b]. Vanilla winters are mild enough that insulation only matters for overheating. Here winter is cold enough that what you wear, where you shelter and how you heat it decide whether you get through. Rooms hold or lose heat by their walls, frost kills crops unless you cover them or grow under a row tunnel, pipes freeze, and frostbite is there if you want it.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] 1.4.0 or newer (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes, dedicated servers included. Every player sees the same weather[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Works with[/b][/td][td]Dazed Plumbing, Dazed Dank, Dazed Butchery, Dazed Cooking, Dazed Power[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedClimate[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-climates.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/climates.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Realism[/b]: Kentucky weather. Winter days about 5 °C, nights about -4 °C, cold snaps down to -10 to -20 °C. Around 80 frost nights a year.
[*][b]Harsh Reality[/b]: deep northern winters, about -7 °C by day and -17 °C by night, with arctic outbreaks down to -25 to -40 °C. Around 170 frost nights a year.
[*]Temperatures swing between night and day, wander day to day, and drift through cold snaps and warm spells over several days.
[*]Pick Vanilla to turn the whole mod off.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-rooms.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/rooms.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Every room near a player has its own temperature, updated every 10 in-game minutes.
[*]Brick, stone and log walls hold heat best, plank and siding less, sheet metal hardly at all. Basements stay near 10 °C.
[*]Open or broken windows and doors let heat out; a barricaded hole much less.
[*]Lit fireplaces and wood stoves, barbecues, a working stove and sun through windows warm a room. Greenhouses catch a lot more sun.
[*]Until the power goes off, houses keep their heating and air conditioning (18 to 25 °C).
[*]A room warmer than outside warms you while you stand in it.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-frost.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/frost.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Outdoor crops are hurt below their frost line and killed by an hour of hard frost. Tender crops go first (0 °C), half-hardy next (-2 °C), hardy last (-5 °C).
[*]Right-click a crop to [b]Cover plant against frost[/b] with a sheet, tarp or blanket: it keeps the plant 4 °C warmer.
[*]Indoor and greenhouse crops are safe.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-tunnels.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/tunnels.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click a farm plot to [b]Put up a row tunnel[/b]: a tarp or 3 garbage bags for the plastic, and 3 sticks or branches for the hoops.
[*]The crop under it is about 4 °C warmer at night and up to 14 °C warmer on a clear noon.
[*]From October to April it skips the game's winter and out-of-season penalties, so you can keep growing through the cold months.
[*]Rain can't reach it: water it by hand.
[*]Tunnels side by side line up into one bed, and a tunnel stays up between crops. Take it down from the same menu.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-ice.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/ice.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Water pipes freeze in about 3 hours at -5 °C and pass nothing until they thaw. [b]Pipe Insulation Wrap[/b] slows that fourfold. Find it in plumbing and hardware stock, or make it from ripped sheets and duct tape.
[*]Water tanks freeze too, slower the bigger they are. A tank that freezes over 80% full may crack and leak once thawed until you weld it.
[*]Petrol and propane never freeze.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-thermo.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/cold.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]A [b]Dial Thermometer[/b], found in kitchens, garages, tool, camping, farm and garden stores, reads the temperature where you stand.
[*]The emergency broadcast gives this mod's temperatures for today and tomorrow, with frost advisories and cold-weather warnings.
[*]Food in a room below 15 °C ages slower: about fridge speed at 0–4 °C, almost not at all when frozen. A cellar or an unheated room in winter becomes a larder.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-frostbite.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Cold hands and feet build up frostnip, then frostbite, shown in the Health panel. Gloves, boots and wet clothes all matter.
[*]Frostnip heals once warm. Frostbite needs warmth and a bandage; left bare it can blister open and get infected.
[*]Frostbite left cold costs a finger or a toe for good. Each lost finger slows your actions, each lost toe your walking.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-sandbox.png?v=2[/img]
On the Dazed Climate page: climate, winter and summer shift, day-to-day variability, weather seed, room temperatures, feeling the room, grid heating, crop frost, row tunnels, frozen pipes and tanks, tank crack chance, radio forecasts, frostbite and its speed, and cold storage. The Dazed Core preset (Easy, Standard, Realistic, Hardcore) also sets the climate and variability.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-compat.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only.
[*]Climate steers the game's own outdoor temperature, so it may not mix with other mods that change temperature.
[*][b]Dazed Plumbing[/b]: frozen pipes and tanks. [b]Dazed Dank[/b]: cannabis feels frost through its own care and stress. [b]Dazed Butchery[/b]: carcasses spoil and dry-age by room temperature. [b]Dazed Cooking[/b]: hot food and drinks warm you. [b]Dazed Power[/b]: rooms a room cooler keeps cold are left to it.
[*]Thermometer and radio follow the Temperatures choice (Celsius or Fahrenheit) on the Dazed Core options page with Dazed Core 1.6.0 or newer; otherwise the game's own display setting.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Climate/images/h-help.png?v=2[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

